# class: integration-tests
# schema: section | title | kind | summary | source
# source: docs/integration-tests.md
# recipe: novel
# authored: 2026-05-23
# reindexed: 2026-05-24 (WireMock JVM consolidation: updated image tag sheyenrath/wiremock.net:2.4.0 -> wiremock/wiremock:3.10.0; WireMock.Net -> JVM WireMock wording; fixed stale anchors for §4/§5/§8/§9 renumbering)
# Recipe: per H2 section extract id, title, kind (purpose / topology / admin-API / mappings / scenarios / runtime / workflow), one-line summary, source anchor. Admin-API subsections (POST /__admin/mappings/import, /reset, GET /__admin/requests) and scenario-bundle co-location story (testing/fixtures/gha/scenarios/ + demo/) are first-class rows so consumer roles can cite individual contract surfaces.

purpose | Purpose + audience | purpose | Verify inbound write path end-to-end (Dashboard.Fetcher -> mock GHA -> fetcher poll -> POST /api/deployments via gateway -> Postgres -> NOTIFY/LISTEN -> SSE); asserts FR-06 wire shape, NFR-03 5s latency, NFR-05 stateless replica restart, ADR-0004 cursor contract | @docs/integration-tests.md#1-purpose--audience
two-doc-context | Two-doc context — three CI/CD axes | purpose | Third axis alongside ci-cd-pipelines.md (outbound) + ci-cd-integration.md (inbound); cross-stack runtime verification of the fetcher's pull-mode path against a deterministic upstream | @docs/integration-tests.md#2-two-doc-context--three-cicd-axes
stack-topology | Stack topology under the integration profile | topology | mock-gha container (wiremock/wiremock:3.10.0) on internal Docker network; host admin port 18080->80 only under integration profile per NFR-04; fetcher retargeted via GHA_API_BASE_URL=http://mock-gha:80; FETCHER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1 | @docs/integration-tests.md#3-stack-topology-under-the-integration-profile
admin-api-import | Admin-API surface — POST /__admin/mappings/import | admin-API | Runner activates scenario via POST /__admin/mappings/import to load JVM WireMock mapping bundles into mock-gha at test time; single-body or directory import | @docs/integration-tests.md#admin-api-surface
admin-api-reset | Admin-API surface — POST /__admin/mappings/reset | admin-API | Reset mock-gha to its startup mapping state; used between scenarios to ensure isolation | @docs/integration-tests.md#admin-api-surface
admin-api-requests | Admin-API surface — GET /__admin/requests | admin-API | Retrieve list of requests mock-gha received; used by test runner to assert the fetcher called the expected endpoints per scenario | @docs/integration-tests.md#admin-api-surface
profile-gating | Profile gating — integration vs demo profiles | topology | Two non-overlapping compose profiles: integration (starts mock-gha; bind-mount; runner-side scenario activation) + demo (starts demo-gha; baked bundle; no admin port per CR-0013); same compose project; fetcher GHA_API_BASE_URL resolves to different DNS under each | @docs/integration-tests.md#profile-gating
two-profiles-two-bundles | Two profiles, two bundles (§3.1) | topology | integration: mock-gha upstream JVM WireMock image (wiremock/wiremock:3.10.0) + bind-mount testing/fixtures/gha/mappings/ + scenarios/ + runner activates; demo: demo-gha first-party baked image + testing/fixtures/gha/demo/ baked at build time per CR-0013; coexist without competition | @docs/integration-tests.md#31-two-profiles-two-bundles
fixture-corpus-mappings | Fixture corpus — testing/fixtures/gha/mappings/ | mappings | Per-endpoint base mappings (one file per (method, URL pattern), filename-prefix ordered for priority); loaded at mock-gha startup under integration profile | @docs/integration-tests.md#fixture-corpus--testingfixturesgha
fixture-corpus-scenarios | Fixture corpus — testing/fixtures/gha/scenarios/<state-id>/ | scenarios | Per-state scenario bundles (one directory per canonical box state from ui-states.yaml); six states: success, running-with-last, running-failed-with-last, failed-with-last, running, running-failed | @docs/integration-tests.md#fixture-corpus--testingfixturesgha
fixture-corpus-cross-cutting | Fixture corpus — testing/fixtures/gha/scenarios/_cross-cutting/ | scenarios | Cross-cutting scenarios (NFR-05 replica restart; ADR-0004 cursor contract); distinct from box-state scenarios | @docs/integration-tests.md#fixture-corpus--testingfixturesgha
fixture-corpus-demo | Fixture corpus — testing/fixtures/gha/demo/ | scenarios | Demo-mode mapping bundle; authored in CR-0012 but consumed by CR-0013 demo profile; baked into deployment-dashboard-demo-gha image; 6 services × 5+ envs; 80-150 deployments; four DAG-edge shapes | @docs/integration-tests.md#fixture-corpus--testingfixturesgha
six-box-states | Six canonical box states | scenarios | Recanonicalised against ui-states.yaml (not GHA upstream states): success / running-with-last / running-failed-with-last / failed-with-last / running / running-failed; each integration scenario drives exactly one canonical box state | @docs/integration-tests.md#six-canonical-box-states
wiremock-admin-api-pattern | JVM WireMock admin-API activation pattern | admin-API | Test runner: POST /__admin/mappings/import to activate scenario; wait FETCHER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1 + buffer; GET /api/deployments + SSE assertions; POST /__admin/mappings/reset between tests | @docs/integration-tests.md#5-scenario-activation-via-admin-api
local-run | Running the suite locally | runtime | dev_env/start.ps1 -Integration; then testing/integration/run-tests.ps1; host-mapped admin port 18080 available to runner | @docs/integration-tests.md#8-local-dev--integration-switch
integration-ci | CI workflow (integration.yml) | workflow | .github/workflows/integration.yml; starts stack with integration profile + runs cross-stack suite; severity: watching-week non-blocking per CR-0012 §3e then promoted to blocking after one calendar week of green runs | @docs/integration-tests.md#7-ci-invocation----githubworkflowsintegrationyml
severity-posture | Severity posture — non-blocking watching week | workflow | integration.yml starts as non-blocking to gather signal; branch-protection promotion is a repo-settings change (not workflow-config) once stable | @docs/integration-tests.md#73-severity-posture--non-blocking-watching-week
adding-scenarios | Adding new scenarios | mappings | Create scenario bundle directory under testing/fixtures/gha/scenarios/<state-id>/; add JVM WireMock JSON mapping files per endpoint (camelCase keys); add corresponding xUnit test case in testing/integration/ that imports + asserts | @docs/integration-tests.md#4-wiremock-mapping-authoring-conventions
troubleshooting | Troubleshooting the integration suite | runtime | Common failure modes: FETCHER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS not=1 (slow test); admin port 18080 not published (integration profile not active); fetcher GHA_API_BASE_URL still https://api.github.com (override not applied); JVM WireMock mapping priority conflicts | @docs/integration-tests.md#9-six-canonical-box-state-inventory
future-work | Future work | runtime | demo-mode integration path via demo profile; additional cross-cutting scenarios (rate-limit-hit + ADR-0008 leaky-bucket gate); NFR-03 latency assertion tightening | @docs/integration-tests.md#10-future-work
